  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Rapidly absorbed with a mean absolute bioavailability of 41%; a high-fat meal slows absorption. About 96% is bound to plasma proteins and clearance is mainly hepatic via CYP3A4.",
    "substance": "Supplied as the citrate salt, molecular weight 666.7 against 474.6 for the free base. Its solubility in water is 3.5 mg/mL.",
    "product": "Marketed under an NDA as film-coated tablets of 25, 50 and 100 mg.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning. Contraindicated with nitrates and with guanylate cyclase stimulators; headache, flushing and dyspepsia are the leading adverse reactions.",
    "indication": "Indicated for the treatment of erectile dysfunction.",
    "mechanism": "Inhibits phosphodiesterase type 5, which degrades cGMP, so nitric oxide signalling relaxes smooth muscle for longer; its selectivity over the retinal enzyme PDE6 is only about 10-fold."
  },
  "tell": "A PDE5 inhibitor with 41% bioavailability and a nitrate contraindication; the blue diamond tablet is its signature.",
